  <revision rev="3" vrev="1">
    <srcmd5>ef1e3541fc4e44f385730c0be67a2912</srcmd5>
    <version>0.149.1</version>
    <time>1787579041</time>
    <user>anag_factory</user>
    <comment>Update to 0.149.1.

Small upstream release: 5 commits, 23 files. codex exec callers can classify
new threads, retained images are budgeted during remote compaction, and
detached memory requests are identified as memory consolidation.

vendor.tar.zst is carried over unchanged. codex-rs/Cargo.lock is byte-identical
between 0.149.0 and 0.149.1 (upstream's only Cargo.toml change was the
workspace version line, and the workspace members are recorded in the lock as
0.0.0), so re-vendoring with update=false resolves the same crate set. The
Legal-Review-Notice crate tallies in the spec are unchanged for the same reason.

Both patches apply without fuzz. Built green on openSUSE_Tumbleweed/aarch64:
rpmlint 0 errors, 0 warnings, 0 badness; %check 341 tests passed across the five
allowlisted crates; the built binary reports &quot;codex-cli 0.149.1&quot;.</comment>
    <requestid>1373338</requestid>
  </revision>
  <revision rev="4" vrev="1">
    <srcmd5>c6827aeeb7a58f757ec834956881dec2</srcmd5>
    <version>0.150.1</version>
    <time>1787849637</time>
    <user>anag_factory</user>
    <comment>Update openai-codex to 0.150.1.

0.150.0 adds @-mentions of other Codex tasks (agents can read, create
and message tasks from the terminal), a /copy picker for the full
response, code blocks and blockquotes, automatic titles for unnamed
terminal tasks, keybindings for cycling the permission modes, a Vim
repeat-last-edit motion, and Interrupt hooks. It also stops untrusted
projects from supplying project-level AGENTS.md instructions, keeps
managed deny-read rules enforced across permission changes, widens
credential redaction in app-server diagnostics, and fixes remote MCP
bearer-token lookup, Unix shutdown hangs caused by detached processes,
and compaction plus multi-agent support for Amazon Bedrock models.

0.150.1 backports retained-image compaction budgeting to the 0.150
line, restoring the behaviour 0.149.1 already had.

Both downstream patches (codex-drop-v8-code-mode.patch,
codex-no-startup-update-check.patch) were rebased onto 0.150.1; neither
changed in content and both still apply with zero fuzz. Upstream still
declares v8 = &quot;=150.4.0&quot; and still ships the v8-poc, code-mode-runtime
and code-mode-host members, so the first patch is still required.

vendor.tar.zst was regenerated with the procedure documented in
_service: rmcp and rmcp-macros move from 3.1.2 to 3.1.3 and are the
only third-party crate change, and cargo-audit reports the lockfile
clean. The licence audit was redone with cargo tree against the new
vendor tree: rmcp 3.1.3 is Apache-2.0 as 3.1.2 was, and the three new
crates are upstream's own workspace members, so the License: tag is
unchanged and only the crate counts in the Legal-Review-Notice comment
were refreshed (874 on aarch64 / 876 on x86_64, Apache-2.0 647).

Built locally on openSUSE_Tumbleweed/aarch64: rpmlint 0 errors,
0 warnings, 0 badness, and the %check suite green with 349 tests passed.</comment>
